  "reasoning": "The patient presents with significant swelling in the legs severe enough to affect shoe fit, along with discomfort during prolonged sitting. Among the possible diagnoses, varicose veins is the condition most classically associated with lower extremity edema, heaviness, and discomfort exacerbated by prolonged sitting or standing. Other candidates like diabetes (typically presents with thirst and frequent urination), hypertension (headaches, dizziness), and arthritis (joint pain and stiffness) do not align with the isolated complaint of leg swelling and sitting-related discomfort. Multiple training references confirm that complaints of leg swelling and vein-related discomfort map directly to varicose veins.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
